    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "contrast",
      "title": "No V2 Inside the Subordinate Clause",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "V2 means that the finite verb stands in second position in many main clauses. A main clause is a complete sentence part that can stand alone. Subordinate clauses introduced by "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "at",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "fordi",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", and "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "hvis",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " do not use V2 inside the dependent part."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "rule",
          "statement": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Do not move the finite verb before the subject inside a subordinate clause: use "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "fordi hun ikke kan",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": ", not "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "fordi kan hun ikke",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jeg blir hjemme fordi jeg ikke er frisk."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I am staying home because I am not well."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Hun sier at de alltid spiser klokka seks."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "She says that they always eat at six o'clock."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "callout",
          "level": "warning",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "kind": "paragraph",
              "spans": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": "Keep the main clause and the subordinate clause separate in your mind. The main clause may have its own word order, but after "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "at",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": ", "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "fordi",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": ", or "
                },
                {
                  "kind": "foreign_term",
                  "value": "hvis",
                  "lang": "no"
                },
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "value": ", the dependent clause follows subordinate word order."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "section",
      "role": "model",
      "title": "Three Useful Starters",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "spans": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Use "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "at",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " for that, "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "fordi",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " for because, and "
            },
            {
              "kind": "foreign_term",
              "value": "hvis",
              "lang": "no"
            },
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": " for if. The starter changes the meaning, but the order inside the subordinate clause stays the same."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Jeg tror at hun ikke jobber i kveld."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "I think that she is not working tonight."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Han kommer sent fordi toget ikke går nå."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "He is coming late because the train is not running now."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "example",
          "no": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "Vi lager kaffe hvis du ikke vil ha te."
            }
          ],
          "en": [
            {
              "kind": "text",
              "value": "We will make coffee if you do not want tea."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "at",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " introduces what someone thinks, says, knows, or believes."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
                "value": "fordi",
                "lang": "no"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " gives a reason."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "kind": "foreign_term",
